diff --git a/docs/victoriametrics/relabeling.md b/docs/victoriametrics/relabeling.md
index a5ac86e..a717641 100644
--- a/docs/victoriametrics/relabeling.md
+++ b/docs/victoriametrics/relabeling.md
@@ -299,6 +299,19 @@ Beside enhancements, VictoriaMetrics also provides the following new actions:
 
   [Try the above config](https://play.victoriametrics.com/select/0/prometheus/graph/#/relabeling?config=-+action%3A+drop_metrics%0A++regex%3A+%22go_gc_duration_seconds%7Cprocess_cpu_seconds_total%22&labels=%7B__name__%3D%22go_gc_duration_seconds%22%2C+job%3D%22go-app%22%7D)
 
+- **`trim` action**: Strips leading and trailing whitespace from the value of
+  `source_labels` (after joining them with `separator`) and writes the result
+  to `target_label`. This is useful for cleaning up label values that pick up
+  stray whitespace from their source (e.g. a trailing newline), without having
+  to hand-craft a regex-based `replace` rule. Example: trim whitespace from the
+  `pod_name` label:
+
+  ```yaml {hl_lines=[1]}
+  - action: trim
+    source_labels: ["pod_name"]
+    target_label: "pod_name"
+  ```
+
 - **`graphite` action**: Applies Graphite-style relabeling rules to extract
   labels from metric names
   ([Try it](https://play.victoriametrics.com/select/0/prometheus/graph/#/relabeling?config=-+action%3A+graphite%0A++match%3A+%27*.server.*.total%27%0A++labels%3A%0A++++__name__%3A+%27%24%7B2%7D_total%27%0A++++instance%3A+%27%24%7B2%7D%3A9100%27%0A++++job%3A+%27%241%27&labels=%7B__name__%3D%22app1.server.requests.total%22%7D)).
